EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Lion_and_the_Lily_AnjouAndAquitaine_LunaANobleRat" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Lion and the Lily - Luna: A Noble Rat"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Lion_and_the_Lily_Core_Ext"

    # Luna: A Noble Rat (Chapter Six: Anjou and Aquitaine, p75): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #tc5eb4fde487f57e0bb627e ^"Luna: A Noble Rat" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t705be3dc14c782e3c434fa ^"Nidi"]
            ^"Age" STRING "26 (Apparent age 26)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Sly +3, Shy +1"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 75
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Born in Sicily, Luna has the dark hair and eyes common to people of mixed Italian and Arabic ancestry. She is far shorter and slighter than average, just under five feet tall. Luna is in her twenties, and prefers clothing with a minimal number of layers, so that she can slip into and out of her heartbeast more easily. She does not have a talisman yet, and is looking for a suitable object to enchant.\n\nLuna lives at Conventio Nidi because her Housemates consider her a freak. She trained, initially, in the Beast Master tradition within House Ex Miscellanea. Micropedus was able to draw out her heartbeast and have her accepted, if not respected, as a member of his House. Heartbeasts are supposed to be wild and noble, but Luna’s is a rodent. She feels that rats are noble creatures: sneaky, tenacious, and durable. They are also perfectly suited to life alongside humans, who are messy and wasteful, but skilled at making small, dark, dry spaces near food.\n\nLuna has developed a psychological quirk. She spends at least an hour per week sitting, in her heartbeast form, on a rafter near the roof of the granary that feeds the covenant. She stares down at all of the food, more than a rat could eat in a century, as the impulses in her rat brain tell her that life cannot be better, or more surprising, than this. Luna also does this whenever she feels stressed.\n\nLuna’s strongest Art is Animal, although her studies have not been as focused as those of other magi. She has learned the Arts she requires to study certain tricks she finds useful. She has mastered a spell that allows her to tunnel through stone or wood while in rat shape. Her combat spells are poor, but she has retained her original tradition’s ability to call and command animals, so she can defend herself with hordes of rats."
    }

}
